# DescartesOS

## Getting Started

DescartesOS is a Custom ROM Based on Android 17

This guide walks you through setting up your build environment, downloading the source code, configuring device trees, and building DescartesOS.

---

### Download the Source

Initialize the repository:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/DescartesOS/android.git -b lineage-24.0 --git-lfs
```

Then synchronize the source code:

```bash
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

---

### Set up Build Environment

Follow the standard [LineageOS build guide](https://wiki.lineageos.org/devices/) to install required build packages and host tools for Android 17.

Once dependencies are installed, source the environment scripts:

```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
```

---

## Device Tree Setup

DescartesOS builds on top of LineageOS and crDroid device configurations. Start from a functional LineageOS-compatible device tree.

In your device's product makefile (e.g. `lineage_<device>.mk`), inherit the common telephony and device configuration:

```make
$(call inherit-product, vendor/lineage/config/common_full_phone.mk)
```

---

## DescartesOS Device Properties

DescartesOS provides native properties exported to "About Phone" / Hardware info and the Atelier customization dashboard.

Define these in your device tree makefile:

```make
# Maintainer name (underscores in values convert to spaces in UI)
DESCARTES_MAINTAINER := lostsignal-502

# Processor / SoC model
DESCARTES_PROCESSOR := Snapdragon_8_Gen_3

# Battery capacity and technology
DESCARTES_BATTERY := 5000_mAh

# Display specification
DESCARTES_DISPLAY := 6.78_AMOLED_120Hz

# Camera sensor resolutions (comma-separated for multi-lens setups)
DESCARTES_CAMERA_REAR_INFO := 50,48,32
DESCARTES_CAMERA_FRONT_INFO := 32

# Build release type (OFFICIAL, UNOFFICIAL, NIGHTLY)
DESCARTES_BUILD_TYPE := OFFICIAL
```

These are automatically converted into system properties at compile time (`ro.descartes.maintainer`, `ro.descartes.soc`, `ro.descartes.battery`, `ro.descartes.display`, `ro.descartes.camera.rear`, `ro.descartes.camera.front`, `ro.descartes.buildtype`).

---

## Build Configuration & Flags

### Google Mobile Services (GMS)

DescartesOS includes integrated Evolution-X GMS support. You can configure GMS inclusion in your build:

```make
# Enable GMS in the build
WITH_GMS := true

# Optional GMS bundle variants (if WITH_GMS := true):
# Default builds include gms_full.mk. You may override:
TARGET_USES_MINI_GAPPS := true    # Includes gms_mini.mk
TARGET_USES_PICO_GAPPS := true    # Includes gms_pico.mk
```

---

### Firmware & Hardware Feature Flags

Tweak optional features in your device makefile according to device hardware capabilities:

```make
# Face Unlock (Biometrics)
TARGET_FACE_UNLOCK_SUPPORTED := true

# Device as USB Webcam (UVC)
TARGET_BUILD_DEVICE_AS_WEBCAM := true

# Quick Tap gesture support (Columbus)
TARGET_SUPPORTS_QUICK_TAP := true

# Hardware and window blur effects
TARGET_ENABLE_BLUR := true

# Disable MatLog logging prebuilt
TARGET_DISABLE_MATLOG := true
```

---

## Building DescartesOS

### Configure Target Device

Select your device build variant:

```bash
breakfast <device_codename> [user|userdebug|eng]
```

Or configure via `lunch`:

```bash
lunch lineage_<device_codename>-userdebug
```

### Compile the ROM

Start the build:

```bash
brunch <device_codename>
```

Or manually invoke Soong/Ninja:

```bash
m bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

---

## OTA & Updates

DescartesOS Updater looks for official updates and changelogs hosted on the DescartesOS GitHub organization:
- OTA Manifest: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DescartesOS/OTA/lineage-24.0/{device}.json`
- Changelogs: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DescartesOS/OTA/lineage-24.0/changelogs/{device}.txt`
- Firmware & Recovery downloads: [DescartesOS/OTA Releases](https://github.com/DescartesOS/OTA/releases)

